<task id="012" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Preserve deep link through the login redirect</title>
    <phase>1 Hosting migration + routing</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-adjacent SPA change</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Standard MSAL state handling</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="shares App.tsx/auth with 011">false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>frontend, auth, react</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 dev-day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Carry an emailed deep link (e.g. `/project/{id}`) through the MSAL login redirect via `state` and/or `redirectStartPage` and restore it on return, so an unauthenticated user lands on the intended route AFTER authenticating instead of on `/`. Only restore in-app relative paths, guard against redirect loops, and keep the sessionStorage MSAL cache and the broker-only redirect flow unchanged.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a React + MSAL front-end engineer working on the Spaarke external-spa auth flow.
    You follow existing external-spa auth conventions and do not redesign the UI or change the IdP.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Ensure an emailed deep link (e.g. `/project/{id}`) lands the user on the intended route
    AFTER authentication, by carrying the intended path through the MSAL login redirect
    (`state` and/or `redirectStartPage`) and restoring it on return.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      With BrowserRouter (task 011), an unauthenticated hit on `/project/{id}` triggers
      `AuthGuard`'s `loginRedirect`, which navigates away to Entra and returns to the app's
      redirect URI — currently losing the originally requested path (user lands on `/`).
      To make emailed deep links usable, the intended route must survive the redirect via
      MSAL `state` (or `redirectStartPage`) and be restored after MSAL finishes processing the
      auth-code response. Phase 1 stays on the EXISTING Entra B2B identity, so any regression
      here is attributable to routing/auth-state handling, not the IdP.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file status="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts</file>
      <file status="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/AuthGuard.tsx</file>
      <file status="reference">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-config.ts (msalInstance + redirect config)</file>
      <file status="reference">src/client/external-spa/src/App.tsx (BrowserRouter + routes from task 011)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">
      SCOPE: token storage. Do NOT change the sessionStorage MSAL cache (ADR-028 external-SPA
      exception) — this task only carries route state through the redirect.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">
      SCOPE: the auth flow. Preserve the broker-only, redirect-based MSAL flow; do NOT switch
      interaction modes or introduce OBO/token exchange. Keep authority/scopes in config
      (do not hardcode) so Phase 2 can repoint to CIAM without touching this logic.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="visual-anchor">
      SCOPE: any interim UI (spinner). Reuse the existing AuthGuard spinner pattern; do NOT
      redesign the loading/redirect UX.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-SPA-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/components/AuthGuard.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Capture the intended route (current `window.location.pathname + search`) when AuthGuard / acquireBffToken triggers a login or token redirect, passing it via MSAL `state` (or set `redirectStartPage`) on `loginRedirect`/`acquireTokenRedirect`.</step>
    <step>On redirect return, read the preserved `state`/start page after MSAL finishes processing the response and navigate (react-router) to the intended route once, replacing history so back-button doesn't loop.</step>
    <step>Guard against redirect loops and against navigating to an untrusted absolute URL — only restore in-app relative paths.</step>
    <step>Verify the default (no deep link) case still lands on `/` and does not double-navigate.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="deeplink-through-login">Unauthenticated hit on `/project/{id}` triggers login redirect; after auth returns, the app lands on `/project/{id}` (not `/`).</test>
    <test name="no-deeplink-default">Unauthenticated hit on `/` returns to `/` after login with no extra navigation.</test>
    <test name="dark-mode-adr-021">The interim redirect spinner renders correctly under `webDarkTheme` (ADR-021).</test>
  </ui-tests>

  <outputs>
    <output>msal-auth.ts + AuthGuard.tsx carrying and restoring the intended route through the login redirect</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An unauthenticated hit on `/project/{id}` returns to `/project/{id}` after the login redirect completes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The default no-deep-link path still returns to `/` after login (negative case — no spurious redirect target).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Only in-app relative paths are restored; an untrusted absolute URL in state is NOT navigated to (negative/safety case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No redirect loop occurs; history is replaced so the browser back button does not re-trigger login.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MSAL token storage remains sessionStorage — unchanged (negative case).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Modify-only task (no new component surface) — no justification block. Still on Entra B2B in
    Phase 1; authority/scopes stay in config so the Phase 2 CIAM repoint does not touch this logic.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
